    "created_at": "2016-07-13T12:55:09Z",
    "updated_at": "2016-07-13T12:55:09Z",
    "body": "I don't believe that's correct. The superconstructor only sets the custom element state to \"custom\" in step 4.3 of [the HTMLConstructor algorithm](https://html.spec.whatwg.org/multipage/dom.html#html-element-constructors), which is not executed during upgrades.\n\nThe spec's setup is preferable in this way since it prevents the following element from being marked custom:\n\n``` js\nclass Bad1 extends HTMLElement {\n  constructor() {\n    super();\n    throw new Error(\"bad\");\n  }\n}\n```\n",
