    "created_at": "2016-07-13T14:08:14Z",
    "updated_at": "2016-07-13T14:08:14Z",
    "body": "I see, after step 4 in the upgrade algorithm, definition's construction stack will contain at least one element. \n\nI am clear with step 10, but I have a question about step 9. I believe that upgrading an element with the following constructor should throw an \"InvalidStateError\" and the element should not be in \"custom\" state. Please correct me if I've missed something.\n\n``` javascript\nclass Bad2 extends HTMLElement {\n  constructor() {\n    super();\n    return 'random';\n  }\n}\n```\n",
